re lies infant Georgios, passed away at 9 months in the month of May...\u003C/p>  ",{"id":199,"html":200},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>\u003Cp>The inscription is dated to the Byzantine period on the basis of the presence of abbreviation marks. The structure of the epitaph is the same as that of IMusCatania 198 (5th–6th century CE), which features the heading \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">μνημεῖον\u003C/span> and the expression \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">ἐνθάδε κεῖται\u003C/span>, followed by the name of the deceased in the nominative (cf. Korhonen 2004, 265).\u003C/p>  ",{"id":202,"html":203},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> 2001 51.1201 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Manganaro 2001 138 fig.3 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001807\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001807\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Korhonen 2004 265 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000028\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000028\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  ",{"id":205,"html":206},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. ",[208,210,213,214],{"html":209},"Text encoding: Jonathan Prag",{"id":211,"lang":99,"html":212},"edition-interpretive","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>❦ \u003Cspan class=\"error\" title=\"hi tag with rend=stacked is not supported!\">𐆌\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"μνημίον\">\u003Cspan class=\"petraeligature\" title=\"Ligature: these characters are joined\">μ͡ν͡η͡μ\u003C/span>(ίον)\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"ἐνθάδε\">ἐνθά[δε]\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"κῖτε\">[κῖτε]\u0